  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Plugin Marketplace",
      "text": "> Browse and install plugins in DeepSeek Harness, and share your usage feedback with the community.\n\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://dshindex.dev)\n\n**English** · [中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it is",
      "text": "[DSH Index](https://dshindex.dev) is a public index of DeepSeek Harness plugins, built from the GitHub [`dsh-plugin`](https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin) topic. **DSH Plugin Marketplace** brings that index into [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness): browse and inspect plugins, install them with your explicit confirmation, and report back to the community.\n\nIt runs inside DeepSeek Harness as a plugin, and ships the same capabilities to the `dsh-index` CLI."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @dshindex/dsh-plugin-marketplace\n```\n\nThen restart `dsh web`. The package ships a host plugin, a Web client bundle, and the `dsh-index` CLI in one bundle."
    },
    {
      "section": "In DSH Web",
      "text": "- **Discover** — search and inspect DSH Index sources, see the current indexed total, and hand an editable `Install plugin <repository URL>` prompt to the Agent.\n- **Report issues** — turn a failure into a redacted GitHub or Gitee Issue draft; review and submit it, then watch its state.\n- **Give feedback** — score a plugin, answer an FAQ, or report a pitfall."
    },
    {
      "section": "In the CLI",
      "text": "The same typed client powers the DSH tools and the `dsh-index` CLI:\n\n```text\ndsh-index doctor\ndsh-index plugins list --query \"git\" --tag workflow --cursor <cursor>\ndsh-index plugins summary\ndsh-index plugins show owner/repo\n\nThe CLI is an interface to the same policy-enforced library, not a route around consent. In Harness, the equivalent abilities are model-callable tools whose side-effecting calls go through the normal user-approval policy."
    },
    {
      "section": "Trust & consent by design",
      "text": "- A `dsh-plugin` topic match is a **discovery candidate**, never a compatibility or safety claim.\n- Every install is a user-confirmed handoff — there is no background install.\n- Issue drafts are redacted before submission; tokens, secrets, source files, and raw transcripts are excluded by default.\n- Scores and reports stay private until the author opts in and DSH Index approves them.\n- Issue polling is local and conservative, using conditional reads and backoff."
    },
    {
      "section": "Relationship to DSH Index",
      "text": "| Product | Responsibility | It does not do |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [DSH Index](https://dshindex.dev) | Public discovery, daily snapshots, observed movement, and moderated community reference | Certify a repository, audit security, or recommend an installation |\n| Marketplace | DeepSeek Harness action layer: search, inspect, user-confirmed install, issue drafts/status, and contributions | Silently install packages, silently file issues, or publish raw user data |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run check   # build + 100% coverage tests\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT. See [LICENSE](LICENSE)."
    }
